I have enough signal. Here are the gaps I found that are **from the refactor itself** (not in TD files, not the Resend integration).


## Deploy / local-dev path regressions

5. **Per-app local-dev deploy is gone.** Old `platform/packages/deployer/src/cloud-run-dev.ts` did `docker run` on the compose network so a generated handler could be tested locally. New deployer has `DEPLOY_MODE=local` only in `build-image.ts` (the image builds) — `cloud-run-ops.ts` and `orchestrator.ts` don't branch on it and unconditionally call Cloud Run Admin. The "Step 9 — Deploy" section of `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` ("Build and start the harness Docker container → `functionUrl: http://localhost:9002`") no longer works.
6. **`docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` was only partially updated for the refactor.** Admin URL fixed (`/admin-ui/...` → `/admin/...`), but Step 9 still says "Build and start the harness Docker container", Step 13 says `docker logs harness-00000000-...`, and the Quick-reference table lists "widget proxy" under the API. All describe the deleted single-harness model.

## Silently-dropped safety features on the edge

8. **Rate limiting is gone on both public services.** Old webhook-gateway: `@fastify/rate-limit` + Redis, 200/min per `(tenantId, appId)`. Old API: 100/min per tenant. New webhook-gateway never registers the plugin (yet still lists `@fastify/rate-limit` in `package.json` — dead dep). New API has no `ioredis` or rate-limit dep at all. Only Fastify's `bodyLimit` + Cloud Run concurrency protect from abuse.
9. **Metrics plugin deleted.** Old webhook-gateway had `plugins/metrics.ts` emitting `type: "http_request"` structured logs (method, route, statusClass, durationMs) for log-based metric aggregation. Gone — no replacement on either service.
10. **Error handler downgraded.** Old webhook-gateway had a full `plugins/error-handler.ts` returning clean 400s for validation errors and sanitising 500s. New webhook-gateway has a 3-line inline handler that returns `{ error: "internal_error" }` for anything ≥500.
11. **Per-handler timeout enforcement lost.** Old `platform/packages/harness/src/timeout.ts` wrapped handler execution in a timeout. The new `templates/handler/` has no Express request-timeout middleware; only Cloud Run's 30 s hard cap catches runaway handlers.

## Infra-pipeline holes

12. **`platform-shopify-admin` is not built or deployed by CI.** `platform-front` has the full Vite-build + `gcloud storage rsync` step. `platform-shopify-admin` — the iframe Shopify Admin actually loads when a merchant opens the app — has no CI job, no bucket, no deploy YAML, not even an `API_URL` injection. The iframe-contract fix (`0897350`) is code-complete but unshippable today.
13. **Stale package reference in frontend types** — `platform-front/src/types/dashboard.ts:1` says `// Mirrors the subset of @new-one-two/types needed by the dashboard.` The old monorepo `@new-one-two/*` package namespace was renamed to `@platform-back/*`. Just a comment, but it's the tell that sections of `dashboard.ts` haven't been re-audited against the new types.

## Carry-over scale issues the refactor made worse

14. **Deploy job state lives in a per-process `Map` in `orchestrator.ts`.** Old deploy was sync-in-request so it didn't matter; new deploy returns a `jobId` and the dashboard subscribes via SSE. With `maxScale: 10` on the API Cloud Run service and no sticky routing, the merchant's SSE connection will hit a different instance from the one running the deploy and see nothing. TD-001 tracks the UI wiring but not this state problem.
15. **Pub/Sub progress fan-out has the same per-process subscription problem** (`pubsub/progress-subscriber.ts`). Present in the old design too, but in the refactor there are now *two* long-lived SSE streams (generation + deploy) running on a service configured to autoscale.

